{"name":"Five Star","hex":"#ffaa4a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"five-star","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the best quality."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard slap on bare skin with a hand that leaves a red, fully hand-shaped mark.","A mark from such a slap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/five-star"}],"entries":[{"title":"Star (classification)","blocks":[{"text":"Star ratings are a type of rating scale using a star symbol or similar typographical mark. It is used by reviewers for ranking things such as films, TV shows, restaurants, and hotels. For example, a system of one to five stars is commonly used in hotel ratings, with five stars being the highest rating."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star_(classification)","wikidata":"Q1642648"},{"title":"Hotel rating","blocks":[{"text":"Hotel ratings are often used to classify hotels according to their quality. From the initial purpose of informing travellers on basic facilities that can be expected, the objectives of hotel rating have expanded into a focus on the hotel experience as a whole. The terms \"grading\", \"rating\", and \"classification\" are used to generally refer to the same concept."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/5_Stars_Superior_DEHOGA_2006-09-06.jpg/330px-5_Stars_Superior_DEHOGA_2006-09-06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hotel_rating","wikidata":"Q2976556"},{"title":"Five Star","blocks":[{"text":"Five Star were a British pop group, formed in 1983 and comprising siblings Stedman, Lorraine, Denise, Doris, and Delroy Pearson. From 1985 to 1988, Five Star had four top-20 albums and 15 top-40 singles in the UK, including the top-10 hits \"System Addict\" (1986), \"Can't Wait Another Minute\" (1986), \"Find the Time\" (1986), \"Rain or Shine\" (1986), \"Stay Out of My Life\" (1987) and \"The Slightest Touch\" (1987). They won the 1987 Brit Award for Best British Group."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Star","wikidata":"Q1421891"},{"title":"Five Star (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Five Star is a 2002 Indian Tamil-language coming-of-age film written and directed by Susi Ganesan in his debut, and produced by Madras Talkies. The film stars newcomers Prasanna, Kaniha, Krishnakumar Ramakumar, Sandhya, Mangai, and Karthik. The film had an ad campaign for 5 Star, which was seen during the interval and end credits. The film was later remade in Telugu as Lifestyle (2009) with a different climax, which had a similar campaign with Lifestyle."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0a/Five_Star_%28film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Five_Star_(film)","wikidata":"Q3687641"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/The_Leading_Hotels_of_the_World.jpg/500px-The_Leading_Hotels_of_the_World.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/The_Leading_Hotels_of_the_World.jpg/500px-The_Leading_Hotels_of_the_World.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Five-star superior\" rating at the Hotel Vier Jahreszeiten Kempinski in Munich, Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Leading_Hotels_of_the_World.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/5_Stars_Superior_DEHOGA_2006-09-06.jpg/330px-5_Stars_Superior_DEHOGA_2006-09-06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/5_Stars_Superior_DEHOGA_2006-09-06.jpg/330px-5_Stars_Superior_DEHOGA_2006-09-06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Five-star Superior\" rating at the Hotel Vi